    "semantic_summary": "FileSystemService acts as the dedicated data access layer for the file explorer, abstracting complex file system interactions. It manages the state of the currently viewed directory using a BehaviorSubject, providing observable streams for directory contents. Its core responsibilities include navigating the mock file structure and asynchronously retrieving the content of specific files, simulating I/O latency."
